      "comparison": "The byte reference computes complete LF-delimited records within the original file and line limits. Ordered returned Data values are retained through completion and fingerprinted with little-endian 64-bit length framing. Count, summed lengths and sha256 must agree with the release and with the reference.",
      "coverage": [
        "64 KiB +-1 and needle placement crossing chunk ends, 127/128/129 and 255/256/257 span batches, 1 MiB +-1 and larger discarded records, and sparse 256 MiB file cutoff with newline just before, at, and after cap.",
        "CRLF, binary payload, NUL, malformed UTF-8, canonical Unicode spellings, empty and duplicate markers, nonempty markers up to 16,385 bytes, 63/64/65/128 markers, unterminated final record, missing and empty files.",
        "Returned Data survives later callbacks, four other complete file scans and caller-side copy-on-write edits for both copying:true and false.",
        "Cancel before scan or from callback, truncate, overwrite a future chunk, append beyond initial length and atomically replace pathname from callback. Original opened inode was consulted and output stayed ordered."
      ]
    },
    "ffi": {
      "nativeChecks": "27 checks per ABI: real fstat/pread, shared-offset dup, successful subsequent read and caller closes the FDs, write-only descriptor returning status 2, closed and pipe descriptors, cap and packed argument rejection before callbacks, short/past EOF, status 1 on cancellation.",
      "faultInjection": "A standalone derivative executable links the same unmodified production Swift source and immutable Rust archive with an inode-scoped test pread definition. On that synthetic input it substitutes EIO or EINTR once the second 64 KiB chunk is requested; other reads delegate to preadv. Input had 1200 ordered lines. EIO returned the first 256 exactly once, EINTR retried and returned 1200 exactly once. The standard non-injected public-entry and ABI binaries were tested separately."
